Geographic data in data.js
==========================

data.js contains simplified, re-projected geometry generated by
tools/build_data.py from the sources below. It is not covered by the MIT
license in LICENSE.

1. Natural Earth (window.GEO.eu: land, countries, lakes, rivers, seas,
   cities, and every mountain range except the two listed in section 2)
   Derived from Natural Earth 1:10m vector data:
     - ne_10m_land                       5.1.1
     - ne_10m_admin_0_countries          5.1.1
     - ne_10m_rivers_lake_centerlines    5.0.0
     - ne_10m_geography_marine_polys     5.1.0
     - ne_10m_geography_regions_polys    5.0.0
     - ne_10m_lakes                      5.0.0
     - ne_10m_populated_places_simple    5.1.2  (capitals)

   The versions used for each build are recorded in the header of
   data.js and in window.GEO.eu.version.ne, read from each dataset's
   *.VERSION.txt; the list above matches the last build.

   Natural Earth is in the public domain. "Made with Natural Earth.
   Free vector and raster map data @ naturalearthdata.com."
   https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/


2. Hand-drawn polygons in tools/handdrawn.geojson
   (window.GEO.eu.ranges: m:Appennino, m:CordiglieraCantabrica)

   Natural Earth has no polygon for the Apennines or the Cantabrian
   Mountains. Their outlines were typed in by hand as lon/lat vertices
   from general geographic knowledge, and checked visually only against
   Natural Earth's own land and country layers. Nothing was traced from
   any other map.

